{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#150","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#150","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#150\",\"parent_revision\":\"05b7dfb29c9ba5a75fe8ec888b5dd23ca9da6853a62f4dea01ef8f65cb3a3d9e\",\"root_revision\":\"05b7dfb29c9ba5a75fe8ec888b5dd23ca9da6853a62f4dea01ef8f65cb3a3d9e\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Gap\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n#109's analysis defined the **provable-zero** set for an agent `tools:` list \u2014 the only conditions under which skilllint can honestly assert the subagent will not launch:\\n\\n- every entry is an unscoped wildcard, **and/or**\\n- every entry is in the documented unconditional first-filter removal list: `AskUserQuestion`, `EndConversation`, `EnterPlanMode`, `ScheduleWakeup`, `TaskOutput`, `WaitForMcpServers`, `Workflow`\\n\\n(`Agent` and `ExitPlanMode` are *conditional* and not statically provable, so they are correctly excluded.)\\n\\nAG001 as shipped in #147 implements only the first half. A `tools:` list consisting entirely of unconditionally-removed tool names still passes lint, though it resolves to nothing and the subagent will refuse to launch.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Not A Defect In 147\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n#147's stated scope was narrower \u2014 port the wildcard check so `tools: mcp__*` stops passing. This is the remainder of the sourced analysis, not a regression.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Prerequisite\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe removal list must be sourced to a cached doc before it is encoded, with the exact quote and line number in the rule docstring. If it cannot be sourced, it must not be added \u2014 an unsourced tool-name set is the AS007 failure this series exists to avoid.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- #109 \u2014 where the provable-zero set was specified\\n- #147 \u2014 implemented the wildcard half\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"9537a47024e115b5f76573d2467267321130ed285f42cae8031583512c842c14\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDORXxKvc8AAAABXP-VuA\"}"}